do GameState.start_minigame()
[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_1.png" fade="1.0" transition="Push Up"]
audio music "res://audio/higheruniversalman-take-me-out-to-the-ball-game-sports-stadium-crowd-music-506221.mp3" [volume="-14.0" loop="true"]
join Valerie midleft
[wait time="1.5"]
Lizzy: I have proof!
Valerie: Alright then.
label Journal Select
do MenuManager.open_journal()
[wait_input]
if {is_success} == true:
	do MinegameTest.update_background("strikes_number")
	if {current_item} == "v_case_study":
		Lizzy: what about that Humprey Egbert the second guy! He had a thing about time loops and para dialation ohanomnminon.
		Valerie: para-dilation phenomenon, yes.
		Valerie: but how could you possibly know that?
		Lizzy: you used it to disprove my time loop theory.
		Lizzy: you also told me he was killed in a sailing accident?
		Valerie: it was never proven a murder, but I have my suspicions...
	
	elif {current_item} == "v_future_worries":
		Lizzy: you didn't always want to be a keeper, but you felt pressured by your father and your grandma.
		Lizzy: It became too much so you dropped out of university,
		Lizzy: and then travelled around Scotland for two years and hung out with sheep.
		Lizzy: Eventually your dad dragged you back and you agreed to work with him.
		Valerie: ...
		Valerie: I don't see how you would know...
		Valerie: Unless you contacted my father, but that's rather unlikely.
	
	elif {current_item} == "pocket_watch":
		Lizzy: well, if I'm not in a time loop, then why do I have your pocket watch?
		Valerie: huh, that's strange. It's not in my pocket...
		Lizzy: yeah, because you gave it to me, for good luck because you thought I was having a mental breakdown.
		Valerie: it's quite lucky.
		Valerie: ...
		Valerie: that is strange.
	
	set {strikes_number} += 1.0
	join Item leftmost [animation="Zoom In" length="9.0"]
	leave Item [animation="Slide To Right" length="1.1" wait="true"]
	if {strikes_number} == 1.0:
		[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_2.png" fade="0.0" transition="Simple Fade"]
	elif {strikes_number} == 2.0:
		[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_3.png" fade="0.0" transition="Simple Fade"]
	elif {strikes_number} == 3.0:
		[background arg="res://assets/Minigame/Minigame_4.png" fade="0.0" transition="Simple Fade"]
	[wait time="1.5"]
else:
	Valerie: What does this have to do with your time loop theory?
	Lizzy: Nothing, just wanted to show you.
	Valerie: ...
	[V.O] I'll have to try something else.
set {is_success} = false
if {strikes_number} < 3.0:
	jump Journal Select
[background fade="2.0" wait="true"]
audio music - [fade="4.0"]
Valerie: A time loop?
Valerie: Now this is troubling...
Lizzy: This is what I've been dealing with.
Valerie: Well, I'm sure we can figure this out together.
do GameState.end_minigame()
jump midpoint_2/